IMPORT prelude

-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1087: the right side of a RAND is still being held to the
-- events after the left side has been breached. `l4 run` on `(WAITUNTIL 3)`
-- gives `BREACH BY Buyer`; on `(WAITUNTIL 3) (WAITUNTIL 6)` it gives
-- `BREACH BY Buyer BY Seller`: the seller's deadline passing adds the seller's
-- blame. The explorer used to stop at the first breach and never reach that.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Buyer, Seller
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF pay, deliver

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
sale MEANS
        (PARTY Buyer MUST pay WITHIN 2 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Buyer)
  RAND  (PARTY Seller MUST deliver WITHIN 5 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Seller)

#TRACE sale AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT 0
